  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 159 PM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nThe rest of the day will be similar to yesterday, a combination of \nheat advisory and extreme heat warning remain in effect through 7pm \nthis evening, the slowly meandering tropical storm Bertha remains \njust of the Gulf Coast, allowing for isolated convection mainly \nacross the southeastern portions of the CWA. Northerly to \nnortheasterly breezes will increase, but will provide little relief \nfrom the heat and humidity, however. Meanwhile, ridging aloft and \nincreasing moisture at the surface, particularly along the \nMississippi River valley, will support peak heat index values of \naround 110 to 115 degrees at most locations through today, with \nvalues remaining around 105 to 110 through Saturday.  At least some \nlimited heat stress is expected for Friday and Saturday, and then \nexpanding influence from the ridge aloft is likely to push us back \ninto Elevated and Significant heat stress by early next week. A cool \nfront stalling in the region today will serve as a focus for \nafternoon shower and thunderstorm development into the weekend. \n/KP/NF/",
